{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id507881788"}, "name":{"label":"rdjmacklin"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-06-05T12:24:56-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.8.2"}, "id":{"label":"11347291381"}, "title":{"label":"Great, but room for even greater."}, "content":{"label":"Love the app, great for managing ADHD driven scrolling habits and aligning with how I want to engage with my phone. Would LOVE custom prompts for the journal entries though - the premade prompts are ok, but being able to enter my own would be fantastic!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=1532875441&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id809508506"}, "name":{"label":"cryyptid"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-05-24T09:09:02-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.8.2"}, "id":{"label":"11302316030"}, "title":{"label":"I hate how well this works."}, "content":{"label":"I’ve only been using this app for about a week, and yet I’ve already noticed that the time spent on my target app is greatly reduced. It really does make you stop and think about what’s really important to you in the moment. And the forced breathing exercise is so annoying (as it’s supposed to be) that I’m noticing I’m not even trying to open the app half as often as I normally would. Also, being told how many times you’ve tried to open the app in a 24 hour period really puts things in to perspective. My compulsive scrolling habits were so much worse than I thought they were, but I’m seeing improvement already! Watching the number of attempts go down over time is quite satisfying.\n\nIf you do need to switch away from the app for a moment it is annoying in the free version to have to go through the exercise again, but the intentional app switching feature in pro helps. Of course, if you don’t actually have a reason to need to come back right away, making it annoying on purpose is good too.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=1532875441&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id1292632356"}, "name":{"label":"AGooseThatLikesBread"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-05-24T00:45:13-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.8.2"}, "id":{"label":"11300892066"}, "title":{"label":"Great App, needs UI polishing"}, "content":{"label":"Excellent app for those who need some friction to prevent them from doomscrolling. My biggest complaint is the UI, it is extremely confusing. The descriptions are vague and it is difficult to tell what a lot of the functions under the customization tab even do. The biggest source of confusion comes from adding apps to block, as the app seems to use the screen time API alongside the shortcuts. Overall, I love the app but would like to see an overhaul of the UI so I can understand how to use this app in a way that is best suited for me.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=1532875441&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
